# Cloudflare-related domains routed through Amnezia.
#
# Why a separate category: Cloudflare's dash + login flow grew its own
# little fan-out (RUM telemetry on a *different* TLD, plus DataDog
# intake), and one of the entries below is a tricky sibling-label
# trap. Keeping them together makes it easy to disable the whole
# group as a unit (rename the file and run vpngw-update-domains.sh).

# Core: dash, docs, workers, challenges (Turnstile). Covers all
# *.cloudflare.com. Without VPN the ISP route to CF edge is unstable —
# Turnstile returns 403 on dash.cloudflare.com; through Amnezia ok.
cloudflare.com

# Cloudflare RUM telemetry. Different TLD — the cloudflare.com mask
# above does NOT match this. Without it the login flow hangs because
# the JS waits for an insights beacon that never returns.
cloudflareinsights.com

# Cloudflare ships client-side metrics/logs into DataDog (US5 region):
#   * http-intake.logs.us5.datadoghq.com   — true subdomain, caught by
#     the datadoghq.com mask
#   * browser-intake-us5-datadoghq.com     — NOT a subdomain. It's a
#     sibling label in the .com TLD ("browser-intake-us5-datadoghq" is
#     the entire leftmost label, no dot before "datadoghq"). dnsmasq
#     matches by dot boundaries, so the mask does not catch it —
#     it needs its own line.
datadoghq.com
browser-intake-us5-datadoghq.com
